findings.body:
`DEFAULT_I18N.addFilter` and `addFilterTitle` are now empty strings, and `StatsFilter` passes `addButtonText=''`. The add button therefore renders only the funnel icon, with `title=''` and no `aria-label`. Screen readers will announce an unlabeled button, and sighted users lose the tooltip. The PR also drops the text that identified the control in the UI.

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="105-105"}

::code{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="2068-2073"}

::callout{type="warning"}
If the icon-only design is intentional, the button still needs a non-empty accessible name. Keep the visible text empty and pass a real `aria-label` through `addFilterTitle` or the button itself.

The PR adds `setSearchInput('')` to `handleClose`, but in the single-select branch of the non-inline `SelectOptionsPopover` it removes the `handleClose()` call and keeps only `setOpen(false)`. Choosing an option from `FilterValueSelector` (the path used when editing an existing select filter) no longer clears the search box. Selecting an item calls `setOpen(false)` directly, which does not fire the Popover `onOpenChange` that clears the search. The old search text therefore persists on reopen.

The inline path that `Filters` uses never calls `handleClose`. It calls `onClose` directly, and the inline component unmounts, so the new `setSearchInput` line does nothing for the stats filter bar.

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1276-1277"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The search-reset fix lands on the wrong path. Restore `handleClose()` in the single-select branch so the search clears, and check the inline `onClose` path separately if it also needs it.

The PR adds `data-[state=closed]:!animation-none data-[state=closed]:!duration-0` to three `PopoverContent` elements. Tailwind's utility is `animate-none`, not `animation-none`, so `!animation-none` generates no CSS. `!duration-0` sets `transition-duration`, not the `animation-duration` that tailwindcss-animate uses for the close animation. Neither class suppresses the close animation, so the code does not do what the author intended.

::diff{file="apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx" lines="1202-1208"}

::callout{type="info"}
Using `data-[state=closed]:!animate-none` is the utility that sets `animation: none`. Verify it in the rendered popover before relying on it.
